From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:28:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 65/93] dmaengine: apple-sio: the T6050 description where the
 sleep is described

The T6050 description, which stops the SIO at the sleep's commit, was
in force on the J714s by name. Follow the device tree: the boards that
describe the sleep. The J716c describes it and leaves its SIO disabled,
so nothing changes there.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 drivers/dma/apple-sio.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c b/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
index cb75beb54ae..4c5b0b1627b 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
@@ -697,12 +697,13 @@ static const struct sio_hw_data sio_hw_t6050 = {
 };
 
 /*
- * The T6050 description is in force on the board it has run on. On another T6050 board the
- * node is taken as before: by its generic compatible.
+ * The T6050 description, with its stop at the sleep's commit, is in force on the boards
+ * that describe the sleep. On another T6050 board the node is taken as before: by its
+ * generic compatible.
  */
 static bool sio_t6050_board(void)
 {
-	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s");
+	return apple_t6050_sleep_described();
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id sio_of_match[] = {
